INT. MUSEUM CLOCKROOM - NIGHT

Brass gears the size of cartwheels turn behind glass. A vault door gleams in the corner, unlit. The crew has been here three hours.

NADIA FARRUKH (30s, mastermind) sits cross-legged on a bench, a tablet balanced on her knee. THEO BAPTISTE (40s, safe man, headphones) listens to the vault. KENJI IWATA (20s, climber) hangs upside down from a beam, sandwich in hand. DOT MCALLISTER (60s, forger) knits on a stool, needles clicking.

THEO
(not looking up)
Four more clicks.

NADIA
Take your time.

KENJI
You said that an hour ago.

NADIA
An hour ago you were still on the roof.

DOT
Nobody's bored if they're knitting.

KENJI
I'm not knitting.

DOT
That's your problem.

Theo holds up one finger. The room stills. A gear grinds. Another. Nadia glances at her tablet; a timer reads 02:14.

NADIA
Guard changes in two minutes.

KENJI
Two minutes is nothing.

NADIA
Two minutes is the whole job.

THEO
Shh!

A THUNK from inside the vault. Theo smiles, exhales, and takes off the headphones. He reaches for the handle. Kenji swings down from the beam, drops the sandwich, grabs Nadia's shoulder. Dot sets her needles down. Nadia stands, tablet clutched to her chest, as Theo turns the handle and the door hisses open on a velvet-lined case holding a small silver clockwork bird.

KENJI
That's it?

NADIA
That's it.

DOT
It's smaller than I thought.

THEO
They always are.

KENJI
Can we go?

NADIA
Not yet. Dot, the swap.

DOT
I'm doing it.

KENJI
Hurry up, hurry up.

DOT
You're rushing me, boy.

THEO
He's not rushing you, he's scared.

KENJI
I'm not scared!

NADIA
Everyone breathe.

Dot lifts the bird with tissue and sets a duplicate in its place. Her hands, so slow on the needles, are fast now. Kenji stuffs the real bird into a padded satchel. Theo pushes the vault shut. The timer on Nadia's tablet reads 00:31.

NADIA (CONT'D)
Go. Go.

KENJI
Which door?

NADIA
Roof!

THEO
Roof is blocked!

DOT
Then stairs!

Boots hit the corridor. A roving flashlight beam swings across the clockroom glass. Kenji drops flat. Theo pulls Dot behind a gear housing. Nadia kills the tablet and the room is black.

The beam lingers on the dropped sandwich. Footsteps pause outside. Nobody breathes.

Nadia's voice, very quiet, from nowhere.

NADIA (CONT'D)
Now.

The beam moves on. Kenji springs for the service stairs. Theo and Dot bolt after him. Nadia follows, the bird bouncing in the satchel. The gears keep turning.
